1133,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000080561","entrez_id":["11043"],"uniprot":["Q9UJV3"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a member of the tripartite motif (TRIM) family. The TRIM motif includes three zinc-binding domains, a RING, a B-box type 1 and a B-box type 2, and a coiled-coil region. The protein localizes to microtubular structures in the cytoplasm. Alternate splicing of this gene results in two transcript variants encoding different isoforms. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9UJV3","text":"E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase that plays a role in microtubule stabilization (PubMed:35266954). Mediates the 'Lys-48'-linked polyubiquitination of LRRK2 to drive its localization to microtubules and its proteasomal degradation in neurons. This ubiquitination inhibits LRRK2 kinase activation by RAB29 (PubMed:35266954)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}